      "observed": "In the netlist, J8 (channel 2) connects through R6 to /NET0007, which is tied to bus pins 19 (via R15) and 21 (via R9). J1 (channel 1) connects through R23 to /NET0032, which is tied to bus pins 20 (via R7) and 22 (via R8). Thus channel 1 uses pins 20/22 and channel 2 uses pins 19/21.",
      "expected": "The specification states that channel 1 should use M5Stack bus pins 19/21 and channel 2 should use pins 20/22.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R9–R12 | 0 Ω (jumpers) | Select which M5Stack bus pin (pin 19/21 for ch.1, pin 20/22 for ch.2) supplies PWM1/PWM2"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"7\") (name \"/NET0007\") ... (node (ref \"R15\") (pin \"1\")) (node (ref \"R6\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"R9\") (pin \"1\"))) ... (net (code \"10\") (name \"/NET0010\") ... (node (ref \"J4\") (pin \"19\")) (node (ref \"R15\") (pin \"2\"))) ... (net (code \"15\") (name \"/NET0022\") ... (node (ref \"J4\") (pin \"21\")) (node (ref \"R9\") (pin \"2\"))) ... (net (code \"36\") (name \"Net-(J8-Pin_3)\") ... (node (ref \"J8\") (pin \"3\")) (node (ref \"R6\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"22\") (name \"/NET0032\") ... (node (ref \"R23\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"R7\") (pin \"1\")) (node (ref \"R8\") (pin \"1\"))) ... (net (code \"6\") (name \"/NET0006\") ... (node (ref \"J4\") (pin \"20\")) (node (ref \"R7\") (pin \"2\"))) ... (net (code \"29\") (name \"/NET0042\") ... (node (ref \"J4\") (pin \"22\")) (node (ref \"R8\") (pin \"2\"))) ... (net (code \"34\") (name \"Net-(J1-Pin_3)\") ... (node (ref \"J1\") (pin \"3\")) (node (ref \"R23\") (pin \"1\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the jumpers are populated as intended for a given M5Stack core, PWM1 and PWM2 will be swapped: PWM1 will drive the channel-2 servo header (J8) and PWM2 will drive channel-1 (J1). This reverses pan and tilt unless the servo cables or firmware are adjusted.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a functional anomaly: the PWM channel-to-M5Stack-bus-pin mapping is swapped relative to the specification, so channel 1 uses pins 20/22 and channel 2 uses pins 19/21 instead of the specified 19/21 for channel 1 and 20/22 for channel 2. This would swap pan and tilt when the jumpers are populated as intended."
}

